{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-21 21:24:09 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-22 04:24:09 Indochina Time  \nCoding-Agent: codex  \nSession-ID: 01a0c501-5311-71f0-94e5-033950e0473d\n\nJ0 FROZEN. The revised 372-case corpus is accepted: 209 canonical cases, 31 encode refusals, and 132 decode refusals. Both independent reviews found no byte disagreement; their agreed fixes are present.\n\n- A4 — ADOPT. `with-meta` wraps the outer `dao.jing/list` or `dao.jing/symbol` frame, preserving an items-only frame payload.\n- A5 — ADOPT. Strip only unqualified `:line`, `:column`, `:end-line`, and `:end-column`, at the top level of every metadata map, recursively including metadata carried inside metadata values.\n- A6 — ADOPT. Portable sequential equality makes lists and vectors equal by content; therefore `[1]` and `(1)` in one set are rejected as `equality-collapse`.\n- A8 — ADOPT provisionally. Empty identifier names are valid strings and remain accepted in v1.\n- A9 — ADOPT. Validate before stripping; a lone surrogate under a stripped key is rejected. The decode counterpart is intentionally classified as `invalid-utf8`, documenting its deliberate two-defect construction.\n- A11 — ADOPT. A reduced ratio with denominator `1` remains tag 30 and retains rational kind.\n- P2-1 — ADOPT. A metadata map carrying its own metadata is `malformed-frame` on both encode and decode.\n\nThe `with-meta` frame name remains `clojure/with-meta`, not `dao.jing/with-meta`. The spelling is already established by Boring and the landed stream fixtures; Jing’s profile separation is expressed by its surrounding value frames and normalization rules. No frozen bytes change, so there are no case IDs to revise.\n\nJ1 must still verify that Boring 0.1.30 can realize the outer-wrapper shape. If it cannot, the implementation must construct that already-frozen frame explicitly; it must not alter the bytes or substitute the stream profile’s inline list metadata form.\n\nOne README immutability line:\n\n```text\nThis file is an immutable v1 contract: tests may verify it, never regenerate or overwrite it.\n```\n\nNo owner action is required for J0."}}
